		{
			dependencies: ["3F1C487831920064"]
			description: ["The six casings of Sagittarius A*: tensegrity truss, clamp coil, optical table, membrane vacuum, droplet radiator and shell window coil. They wall every large MAX structure, and each needs a part that only this era makes."]
			icon: "grindless:tensegrity_truss_casing"
			id: "1AD3DB23754CDAD8"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "5E12E5B2CC815B45", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "Sagittarius casings"
			x: 76.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1AD3DB23754CDAD8"]
			description: ["A casing of struts held apart by tension, so that a structure the size of a hall keeps its shape in free fall. It is the frame of every MAX machine and the base of the five casings that follow. An assembler: two &6Exotic Composite Rods&r (the composite line), four &6Horizon Strand Single Wires&r (the strand line), two Chain Lamina Casings, tungsten steel, a UXV sensor and superfluid helium-3, for four casings. Every MAX plant and the Mirror Shell, and the clamp coil, optical table, membrane vacuum, droplet radiator and window coil casings. Rods and wires by ME, the lamina casings from their line; the helium-3 by pipe. Make them in bulk: a plant takes up to 1,800."]
			icon: "grindless:tensegrity_truss_casing"
			id: "7722FB93135ED9DA"
			rewards: [{ id: "32048881B5353C35", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 4L, id: "112CA6B1E88C3A61", item: "grindless:tensegrity_truss_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tensegrity Truss Casing"
			x: 78.5d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7722FB93135ED9DA"]
			description: ["A casing wound with superconducting coil that holds a field against a plasma or a moving mass. The flux clamp, the synchroniser, the injector and the winch use it. An assembler, 400 ticks: a &6MAX Field Coil&r (the coil line), two strand wires, a truss casing, a UXV fluid regulator and a UXV conveyor module, with 250 mB of superfluid helium-3, for two casings. The Horizon Flux Clamp, the Ergoregion Synchroniser, the Mass Stream Injector, the Geroch Winch and the Atom Interferometer Works. Field coils by ME from the coil line; they are the slow part, so keep a stock."]
			icon: "grindless:clamp_coil_casing"
			id: "336DB6C749EFC3DB"
			rewards: [{ id: "1B318378BABD473C", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "3A99CCBE472462C8", item: "grindless:clamp_coil_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Clamp Coil Casing"
			x: 81.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["336DB6C749EFC3DB"]
			description: ["A casing of a stiff, zero-expansion baseplate with a magnetostrictive layer that damps every vibration. Optics set on it stay aligned to a fraction of a wavelength. An assembler, 400 ticks: a &6Zero-Expansion Baseplate&r (the bench line), a &6Laminated Terfenol Stack&r (the Terfenol line), a truss casing and 250 mB of superfluid helium-3, for two casings. The Photon Ring Imager, the Rydberg Array Works, the Cluster Light Furnace, the Horizon Interferometer and the Atom Interferometer Works. Baseplates and Terfenol stacks by ME; the stack is the slow part."]
			icon: "grindless:max_optical_table_casing"
			id: "16C654CDB2FD76BD"
			rewards: [{ id: "52FF0139790A25E0", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "347F27CDB384ACDD", item: "grindless:max_optical_table_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "MAX Optical Table Casing"
			x: 83.5d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16C654CDB2FD76BD"]
			description: ["A casing walled with the superconducting membrane over an extreme-high vacuum liner, with sealed pumps behind it. Whatever must stay clean and cold is built from it. An assembler, 400 ticks: a &6Superconducting Membrane&r (the membrane line), two NEG XHV Casings, a truss casing, a MAX electric pump, two FFKM seals and 250 mB of superfluid helium-3, for two casings. The Gene Ark, the Atom Interferometer Works, the Rydberg Array Works, the Segment Reclamation Works, the Condensate Refinery and the Flux Clamp. Membranes by ME; the NEG casings and the seals from their lines."]
			icon: "grindless:membrane_vacuum_casing"
			id: "16702944B10310E6"
			rewards: [{ id: "74AA2B15F4E6B001", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "7DE54FFF15B29761", item: "grindless:membrane_vacuum_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Membrane Vacuum Casing"
			x: 86.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16702944B10310E6"]
			description: ["A casing that sheds heat by a curtain of liquid tin-lithium droplets falling in vacuum. It is made at Sagittarius A*, because the radiator panel is. An assembler, 400 ticks: two &6Shell Droplet Radiators&r (made at the hole in the droplet radiator works, from a nozzle plate and a collector shell), a truss casing, a UXV fluid regulator and electric pump, tungsten steel plates, two FFKM seals and 250 mB of superfluid helium-3, for two casings. The Accretion Feeder, the Cluster Light Furnace, the Photon Ring Imager, the Geroch Winch, the Flux Clamp and the Nickel-56 Burner. Radiators by ME from the works, which stands at the hole; the rest of the inputs are shipped."]
			icon: "grindless:droplet_radiator_casing"
			id: "1D835DC1BFCFC03A"
			rewards: [{ id: "3BA204229042DB9B", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "15146CA09E40F27D", item: "grindless:droplet_radiator_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Droplet Radiator Casing"
			x: 88.5d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D835DC1BFCFC03A"]
			description: ["A ring of coil and membrane set round a cleanroom glass port. The Mirror Shell has 26 ports, each ringed by these casings, and nothing else uses them. An assembler, 400 ticks: a &6MAX Field Coil&r, a &6Superconducting Membrane&r, two strand wires, a truss casing, two UXV sensors and two FFKM seals, with 250 mB of superfluid helium-3, for two casings. The Mirror Shell takes 398 of them. The Mirror Shell, which closes the age. Make them on a dedicated line fed by the coil and membrane lines; the shell needs about two hundred batches."]
			icon: "grindless:shell_window_coil_casing"
			id: "78B5470262AB3C38"
			rewards: [{ id: "5AEB118ABB9AA129", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 2L, id: "176D7AC48ACD4751", item: "grindless:shell_window_coil_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Shell Window Coil Casing"
			x: 91.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["39410922EEDADAC9"]
			description: ["The wafers, chips and circuits of the era, from the first wafer to the mainframe, and the parts built from them."]
			icon: "minecraft:writable_book"
			id: "7DA50832A003A040"
