			x: 10.0d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DA50832A003A040"]
			description: ["Light squeezed until its noise drops below what any ordinary beam can reach. The &6Squeezed Light Chip&r goes into the mainframe, and the MAX emitter is built around it. It is one of three parts the mainframe needs, and they can be made in any order. The SNSPD fabrication line, with a bonded pump-laser die, an SNSPD, gold dust and superfluid helium. The mainframe and the MAX emitter. Feed the fabrication line by ME; chips are small, so stock a few and send the rest on."]
			icon: "grindless:squeezed_light_chip"
			id: "5910FF92CEC15A2E"
			rewards: [{ id: "113B65BEADB549B4", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "1DB6B458168FE556", item: "grindless:squeezed_light_chip", type: "item" }]
			title: "Squeezed Light Chip"
			x: 12.5d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DA50832A003A040"]
			description: ["Single atoms held in beams of light, one by one, on a die. The &6Tweezer Array Die&r is the logic the mainframe reads its qubits from. It does not depend on the chip or the interposer. A laser engraver, a calibrated lens and a purple glass lens. The mainframe, and the Rydberg array works, which is researched from it. Lenses by ME in matched counts; the engraver returns dies in a chest."]
			icon: "grindless:tweezer_array_die"
			id: "17CBBAAEADB21164"
			rewards: [{ id: "5FC4C428E07A8BBA", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "7FDED9EDDD366B8E", item: "grindless:tweezer_array_die", type: "item" }]
			title: "Tweezer Array Die"
			x: 12.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DA50832A003A040"]
			description: ["The board that joins the chips at millikelvin. The &6Cryo Photonic Interposer&r carries light between them without heating either. It is made on its own, not from the chip or the die. The nuclear demagnetisation line, with a transducer wafer, a millikelvin cryostat module and helium-3/helium-4 mixture. The mainframe. Keep a few of each part per mainframe in a dedicated chest; a big stock gains nothing."]
			icon: "grindless:cryo_photonic_interposer"
			id: "18F41DE9388D684D"
			rewards: [{ id: "30CD7A6501005BD9", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5C233FAA3A69F48D", item: "grindless:cryo_photonic_interposer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Cryo Photonic Interposer"
			x: 12.5d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5910FF92CEC15A2E", "17CBBAAEADB21164", "18F41DE9388D684D"]
			description: ["The only circuit of MAX, and the last one the pack has.     The &6Supracausal Mainframe&r is the end of the staged line: the Photonic Integration Hall takes a shielded quantum module (built from the interposer, tetron dies and squeezed-light chips), 3 tweezer array dies, 7 OpV circuits, programmed circuit 9 and 3,142 mB of superfluid helium-3, and runs 4,800 ticks. The Photonic Integration Hall (see the M1 line in the lines section), superfluid helium-3 and a stock of the parts. Every MAX component, hatch and controller. Three part lines into one hall: give each its own chest so one slow line never starves the others."]
			icon: "gtnn:supracausal_mainframe"
			id: "3BEE68D81D2C0817"
			rewards: [{ id: "3F96CF74225A6C7E", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "13AC629C7C67ED7B", item: "gtnn:supracausal_mainframe", type: "item" }]
			title: "Supracausal Mainframe"
			x: 17.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3BEE68D81D2C0817"]
			description: ["MAX has no assembler of its own, so MAX parts are put together in the &6Assembly Hall&r. It takes many parts at once and does the work of a whole row of assemblers. The hall controller and two OpV hatches that give it MAX voltage, because MAX hatches do not exist yet. Every MAX component, and later the hatches that replace the OpV pair. Parts by ME; the hall hands back one kind at a time, so a pattern provider per component keeps it busy."]
			icon: "gtceu:assembly_hall"
			id: "34FED870BAF8944F"
			rewards: [{ id: "30FF56E65BF22E96", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
